{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfS8P6zoXKajDrWmcb889","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis of the codebase, here's what I found:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity (Order.kt:11) has no status field yet; needs to be added\n- Shipment entity (Shipment.kt:9) already has `ShipmentStatus` enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- Error handling uses sealed `ApiException` with `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) and `ConflictException` (409)\n- ErrorCode enum (ApiError.kt:31) has: ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n- ShipmentRepository (ShipmentRepository.kt) has no `findByOrderId` method - needs to be added\n- Repositories are in-memory using ConcurrentHashMap\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler catches them\n2. Controllers interact directly with repositories (no service layer)\n3. Tests verify both HTTP status and JSON error body using MockMvc + jsonPath\n4. New entities created with 201 CREATED status\n5. Error responses follow standard envelope: `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\"}}`\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` - add `OrderStatus` enum and `status` field\n2. `OrderController.kt` - add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint\n3. `OrderRepository.kt` - no changes needed (find by ID already exists)\n4. `ShipmentRepository.kt` - add `findByOrderId(orderId)` method to query shipments by order\n5. `ShipmentController.kt` - add check to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n6. `ApiError.kt` - add `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` error code\n7. `OrderControllerTest.kt` - add tests for cancel endpoint behavior\n\n**Risks:**\n- Adding `status` field to `Order` is a breaking change to the JSON response; all existing assertions must account for it\n- Atomic consistency: when cancelling, all shipments must be updated together (in-memory so no transaction needed, but order matters)\n- The ShipmentRepository needs to search by orderId; currently only indexed by shipmentId\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone - the ticket clearly specifies all required behavior.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` values. Add `status: OrderStatus` field to `Order` data class.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) if order doesn't exist\n   - Returns order unchanged if it's already CANCELLED\n   - If ACTIVE and all shipments are CREATED or CANCELLED: sets order to CANCELLED, cancels all CREATED shipments, saves and returns it\n   - If ACTIVE and any shipment is CONFIRMED: throws `ConflictException` (409) with `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` code, changes nothing\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to find all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add validation in `create()` to check if the order exists and is CANCELLED; if so, throw `ConflictException` (409) with `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED`.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt**: Add `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` to the `ErrorCode` enum.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests covering:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order succeeds and returns CANCELLED status\n   - Cancelling a CANCELLED order succeeds without changes\n   - Cancelling an order with CONFIRMED shipment fails with 409, changes nothing\n   - Cancelling non-existent order fails with 404\n   - GET `/orders/{orderId}` includes status field\n   - CREATED shipments are cancelled when order is cancelled\n\n**Alternative rejected:** Could avoid modifying existing Order structure by returning status in a wrapper response, but the ticket explicitly requires `GET /orders/{orderId}` to report status, so status must be in the Order entity itself.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Action | DB Changes | Response |\n|------|-------|--------|-----------|----------|\n| Cancel ACTIVE order | orderId | Check shipments, cancel all CREATED | Order status→CANCELLED, shipments status→CANCELLED | 200 OK, cancelled order |\n| Cancel already CANCELLED | orderId | No action | None | 200 OK, same order |\n| Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment | orderId | Validation fails | None | 409 CONFLICT, ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED |\n| Cancel unknown order | orderId | Not found | None | 404 NOT_FOUND, ORDER_NOT_FOUND |\n| Create shipment for CANCELLED order | orderId | Validation fails | None | 409 CONFLICT, ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **OrderControllerTest** (new/modified):\n   - `cancels_active_order_and_returns_cancelled_status` - verifies POST cancel returns 200, order status is CANCELLED\n   - `cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds` - idempotent retry case, POST cancel succeeds second time\n   - `cancel_with_confirmed_shipment_fails_with_409` - POST cancel fails, nothing changes\n   - `cancel_nonexistent_order_fails_with_404` - OrderNotFoundException case\n   - `created_shipments_are_cancelled_when_order_cancelled` - verifies cascading update\n   - `get_order_includes_status` - verify status field appears in GET response\n   - Need to also verify that status appears in create response\n\n2. **ShipmentControllerTest** (new test):\n   - `create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_fails_with_409` - verifies POST /shipments rejects cancelled orders\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":813,"cache_read_input_tokens":21535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":813},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management"